From 0603ac1d29ff199fad53d75750556fe374c0016b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local <local@localhost>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 11:55:03 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 03/18] Split-decode attention: GQA grouping, EXL3_DEC_*
 tuning, Q4W kernel

A program of the split-decode kernel takes 16 query rows, so a multi-token
verify (q_len 8) spreads Qwen's 6-head GQA groups over 3 programs, each
re-reading and re-dequantizing the same K/V. On gfx1201 at 60k context one
layer goes 1961 -> 605 us (q_len 8), 1336 -> 450 (q_len 4) and 550 -> 336
(q_len 1) with the settings below; max error 2e-6.

- EXL3_DEC_GROUP=1: the whole GQA group per program (decode_block_h) and a
  higher split target (decode_split_target: 8 programs per CU at q_len 1, 4
  for verify; EXL3_DEC_SPLIT_MULT overrides). EXL3_DEC_BLOCK_H sets the
  heads per program directly.
- EXL3_DEC_WARPS / EXL3_DEC_STAGES / EXL3_DEC_BLOCK_N override the launch
  shape, each on its own, through one resolver (decode_launch_overrides)
  shared by the eager launch and the BC graph build, so a BC decline keeps the
  tuning. They layer over upstream's attn_decode_config: explicit arguments,
  then the env overrides, then the per-backend/arch defaults. With none set,
  every arch (gfx1100 included) keeps upstream's config.
- EXL3_DEC_Q4W=1: _paged_attn_decode_split_q4w_kernel for 4-bit K/V caches
  (head_dim a power of two >= 128). It loads each tile's packed words once and
  splits the dots into 8 per-nibble partial dots, avoiding the LDS-shuffle
  unpack: 1.2-1.3x at q_len 4-8. Splits past the live count exit before the
  query preparation.
- BC_Attention::configure_slot takes block_h from Python, so the C++ program
  count matches the BLOCK_H the split kernel was compiled with (recomputing it
  with the old rule faulted the GPU). 0 keeps the old rule.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
